{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOfgsKE4d72L9blVYHcO","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to build out the \"00 · Design Tokens\" system's follow-on work entirely inside workspace 03: foundations (color and text styles), the component library, 5 frames, a prototype, and a screenshot verification pass. The reference data is already in hand, so no further reads are needed and the next steps are judgment calls. Building is sequential: styles come before components, and components before frames.\n\nThe brand direction is lime #BBF246 on charcoal #192126 with Lato. I settle on a light-family system with one dark immersive screen: background #F6F7F8, surface #FFFFFF, primary text #192126, secondary #66757C, subtle #98A2A8, line #E8ECEE, lime #BBF246 and lime-dark #A6DC3C, dark surface #232F34 and dark line #33434A. The lime carries primary actions, the current tab, progress fills and highlight chips; charcoal blocks anchor photos and the immersive workout screen. The canvas is 390x844 for every frame.\n\nFoundations come first: paint styles for the palette and text styles for the scale, named Display/32 Black, H1/26 Black, H2/20 Black, Title/17 Bold, Body/14 Regular, Body/14 Bold, Label/11 Bold, Caption/12 Regular and Num/24 Black, with Lato Regular, Medium, Bold and Black loaded once up front.\n\nThe component library follows: Tab Bar (390x76) built from a Tab Item set with State=Active/Inactive, where Active shows a lime 44x30 pill behind the glyph and charcoal label, Inactive stays muted. Button/Primary covers Default, Pressed and Disabled; Button/Lime covers Default and Pressed. Field/Search covers Default, Focused and Disabled at 350x52. Level Tag covers Beginner, Intermediate and Expert. Further sets: Stat Chip, Section Header, Page Header, Workout Card (188x176 photo card with kcal/min overlay and play button), Plan Row (350x70 with 64 thumb, name, progress bar and level tag), Round Row, Day Cell (default/current), Exercise Tile for Explore, Challenge Card, and Analytics Tile variants for calories, training time, heart rate, steps, water, sleep and cycling.\n\nIcon reuse relies on createInstance of the provided component IDs (5:20 search, 5:22 home, 5:24 explore, 5:26 analytics, 5:28 play, 5:36 back, 5:38 timer, 5:42 fire/energy, 5:45 heart, 5:47 steps, 5:50 water, 5:52 sleep, 5:55 calendar), with vector strokes recolored to match each context. Photos come from the hashed image fills as FILL rectangles.\n\nFor the frames, 01_Onboarding is a full-bleed photo hero with a charcoal gradient into a white bottom card holding the headline \"Wherever you are, health is number one\" and the sub \"There is no instant way to a healthy life\", with the provided Button instanced as the charcoal pill CTA. 02_Home is light: greeting and name \"Pramuditya Uzumaki\" with avatar, a search row instanced from the provided Text Field with Icon_Search inside, two Popular Workouts photo cards, and a Today Plan of 3 Plan Rows such as \"100 push ups a day\" at 45% progress, all fitting above the 76px tab bar. 03_Explore is light: \"Explore\" title, a dark banner card with photo and \"Best Quarantine Workout\" plus \"See more >\", a 2x2 Best for you grid of Exercise Tiles, challenge chips and a fast warmup list, scrolling past the fold. 04_Workout is dark charcoal #192126 with a 240px photo header, \"Lower Body Training\", Stat Chips for Time 50 min and Burn 500 kcal, description copy, a Rounds header at 1/3, 3 Round Rows, and a fixed lime \"Let's Workout\" C","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":4034,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":31239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4034}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bc69212-fb2d-4921-bfba-80c85cc