{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOh666KuKOuG5U0TpZt3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The screenshots point to four concrete problems. In 01_Onboarding the status bar notch reads fine against the photo and the \"FITNESS\" label at y=66 does not overlap anything, so I leave that screen unchanged. In 02_Home every plan row shows \"Intermediate\" when Sit Up and Knee Push Up need \"Beginner\"; the level instance inside each plan row is the same variant, so I delete that child in rows 2 and 3 and add a fresh level instance of the Beginner variant at x=350-16-width, y=14. The \"Hand Training\" card also spills past the right edge, since x=210 plus the 188 width lands at 398 on a 390 canvas. I resize both popular-row cards to 168 wide and 208 tall, then bring their children into line: Photo to 168x132, Scrim to 168x132, Play at x=116, the 16px play icon at x=116+11, and Name and Meta each at width 140. I place the cards at x=20 and x=201, which gives a 13px gap and a clean right margin. The thin line under each tab label reads as text underline, so I set textDecoration='NONE' on the tab labels in both variants and on the screen-level instances.\n\nIn 03_Explore the program tiles are 186 tall but spaced 146 apart, so each name collides with the next row's photo and the level tags run into the Challenge header. The challenge cards are 140 wide at 118 spacing, an overlap of 22px, and they merge into one dark band whose text overflows. The \"Fast Warmup\" header sits hidden behind those cards, and the warmup rows run into the tab bar. I rebuild the body: heading at y=56, banner 92 to 180 at 88 tall, \"Best for you\" header at 190, grid row 1 at 226 to 376 and row 2 at 384 to 534 with tiles of 150 (photo 88, name 13, meta 11, level chip 18), Challenge header at 544, cards at 580 to 652, warmup header at 662, and two compact warmup cards of 171x62 at y=690 ending at 752, which clears the tab bar at 766.\n\nIn 04_Workout the two chip icons overlap on the Burn chip; I remove the timer instance inside s2 and place the fire icon at x=186, leaving the 140-wide chips with their 12px gap and the 758 button as they are. In 05_Analytics the calendar cells fit (last ends at 343.5) but the water and sleep tiles sit behind the tab bar and the \"80% of today's goal\" text overflows the lime pill at x=250. I set that text to width 90, right-aligned, and restack the lower content: calendar 108 to 220, tiles 228 to 352, cycling 360 to 480, hr/steps 488 to 600, \"Keep it Up\" 608 to 654, and water/sleep 662 to 766 at 104 tall, which touches the tab bar exactly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":7513,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":150814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7513}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bc69212-fb2d-4921-bfba-80c85ccd3cdb","uuid":"cb6aa3b7-660b-4d3e-9cd1-e7ae700afb69","timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:30:10.487Z","thinking_duration_ms":58644}
