{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOhFQIEZCIf14bJR0cBB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a private inventory of what comes next and then a set of independent calls. The failure comes from setting x on children inside an instance (\"cannot be overridden in an instance: relative-transform\"), which hit the plan-row level tag placement and the card child moves. So I never reposition children inside instances. Instead I resize instance roots only and put all geometry in the masters: Workout Card at 168x208 with photo at 168x132, scrim at 168x132, play at 116,78, name width 140; Program Tile at 171x150 with photo at 171x92, name at y=100 size 13, meta at y=120, level at y=126 x=90. For the Plan Row I build three variants (Level=Beginner, Level=Intermediate, Level=Expert), each holding its own tag instance, and pick the Beginner variant for Sit Up and Knee Push Up and Intermediate for Push Up. I hide the Timer icon inside the Burn chip and add the fire glyph as a sibling outside it. I rebuild 03 and 05 fresh, swap the 02 card instances for new masters at x=20 and x=202, and set textDecoration NONE.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":13119,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":158327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13119}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bc69212-fb2d-4921-bfba-80c85ccd3cdb","uuid":"35cde771-3d76-4724-824f-baadc692c79b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:36:17.176Z","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":311761}
